  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Given,</p><p>Three-digit number to be formed which are divisible by&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math>&nbsp;using the digits&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>8</mn></math>&nbsp;and repetition is allowed,</p><p>Now taking case&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced></math>, where all digits are same, we get</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>ways</mtext></math></p><p>Now taking case&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced></math>, where&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo></math>digit are same and one is distinct, we get</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8594;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>!</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>ways,</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8594;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>ways</mtext></math></p><p>Now taking case&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mn>3</mn></mfenced></math>, where all are distinct, we get</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>6</mn><mtext>&#160;ways</mtext><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>ways</mtext></math></p><p>So, total ways will be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>22</mn></math></p></blockquote>",
